## 3. Registration

How an asset becomes part of the build.

<!-- DERIVED: depends on `adapters.assets`.

     Registry-based stacks (e.g. Flutter's `flutter: assets:`) declare assets
     explicitly — often as a *directory*, which covers everything beneath it.

     Bundler-driven stacks (Vite, webpack, Next, Metro) have no registry at all: a
     file is included because something imports it, or because it sits in a copied
     public directory. In those projects "is this registered?" has no answer, and
     the tooling refuses the question rather than inventing a boolean. -->

